#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""check-imports: layering, public-API and one-wrapper-file rules (contracts 2.4 and 2.5).

- Python packages import only their "Internal deps" (contracts 2.2), and each external library only in its one
  wrapper file (contracts 2.5, python layout 1.4). The packages are found by folder, so a rule applies from the
  day its package lands.
- JavaScript packages import only their "Internal deps" (contracts 2.3), the public entry of another package and
  not its files, @rastai/ui/security only inside apps/web, @rastai/client in apps/web only from the three folders
  frontend layout 1 names, and each library only where contracts 2.5 allows it.
- Rust: cargo-deny and check-deps pin each single-owner crate to its owning crate; this check pins the file
  inside the owner (contracts 2.5 "Enforced owners").
The tables below restate contracts 2.2, 2.3 and 2.5; tools/checks/tests checks that every package those tables
name has a row here.
"""

